AB  - In the era of the Fourth Industrial Revolution, container platforms such as Docker and Kubernetes have become essential, but they also bring new cybersecurity threats. At the same time, training cybersecurity professionals is facing major challenges in terms of cost, time, and the ability to simulate real-world models.This study explores security vulnerabilities and proposes a virtual laboratory model to provide a secure practice environment for students. By leveraging open source virtualization technology (KVM, Virtual Environment - Next Generation), the model allows simulation of complex network environments on moderate hardware. A web-based document management system (integrated with Google Drive) was developed as the test environment.These findings highlight the importance of layered security. The proposed measures (Dockerfile security, Trivy scanning, RBAC) were validated and demonstrated improved resilience. The virtual lab solution also optimized existing hardware, significantly reducing deployment, space, and time costs, and streamlining the debugging process. The research contributes to the understanding of container security and provides practical guidance for software engineers.  © 2025 IEEE.
